--- a shared helper's refusal names the export whose call made the copy
--- mistakes: 8
--- `lookup` and `latest` both reach magpie's helper `_reaching`; the list
--- handed as `latest`'s `upto` makes a copy of the helpers whose `lt` and
--- `lte` compare text with a number. Every refusal names `latest` at its
--- line: the valid `lookup` call, which reaches the helper first, is not
--- blamed (it had been: a copy lowered before its caller's body had no
--- chain on record, and the first export reaching the helper answered)
use magpie, frame
ok = magpie.lookup['nowhere', ['day'], ['x'], ['timestamp']]
log[ok.reason]
bad = magpie.latest['nowhere', ['id']]
log[bad.reason]
